// APNT pool one-transaction verdict factory v1.
//
// Deployment build of the pool-mode historical-record prototype (historical-record). Its source
// digest is checked by the protocol-runtime builder. Chipnet keys are from a
// simulated single-party ceremony: ZERO-VALUE TEST ONLY, never for value.
//
// Target: protocol-design, "Settlement
// and the proof verdict" (the verdict is an immutable NFT of category V that
// commits runBind32 = SHA-256(S), under the pool settlement lock), with the
// 33-transaction ladder replaced by the one-transaction residue verifier.
//
// This lock is the perpetual home of V's minting NFT. It mints the pool proof
// verdicts in the SAME transaction as the verifier graph, and only for the
// statements that graph verified.
//
//   inputs   0..N-1  the verifier graph (N = 11 for the residue construction)
//            N       this factory, holding V with the minting capability
//   outputs  0..M-1  the verdicts: immutable V NFTs under the settlement lock
//            M       this factory, returned
//            M+1     token-free change
//
// Checks (each is one //@check block; the tests remove them one at a time):
//
//   LAYOUT     this is input N; exactly N+1 inputs and M+2 outputs.
//   OWN_TOKEN  this input's token is V with the minting capability.
//   GRAPH_ROOT input 0's locking bytecode is the pinned root of the verifier
//              graph. Each graph input pins its successor's locking bytecode
//              and the last three pin their positions, so the root fixes all N
//              programs: the SP1 wrapper key, the program key s0 (folded into
//              the terminal's fixed pairing factor), and the zero exit code and
//              zero nonce (their IC terms are absent from the MSM).
//   VERDICTS   outputs 0..M-1: token category exactly V (an immutable NFT: a
//              mutable or minting NFT's category carries a capability byte), no
//              fungible amount, the settlement lock, at least the value floor,
//              and a commitment of the size the mode requires.
//   STATEMENT  the verdict commitments determine the wrapper's public scalar
//              s1. In pool mode s1 = SHA-256(C_0 ‖ … ‖ C_{M-1}) with the top
//              three bits cleared: SP1 6.3.1's hash_bn254 of the aggregate's
//              public values, which are exactly the M runBind32 values in output
//              order. Input 0's unlocking bytecode must then begin with
//              0x4c84 ‖ LE32(s1) ‖ LE32(s3): the push of the 132-byte GLV genesis
//              blob from which the graph's MSM takes its two runtime scalars,
//              s3 being SP1 6.3.1's recursion key root, pinned here.
//   FACTORY    output M returns this input's token (V, minting) to this input's
//              locking bytecode, with an empty commitment, no fungible amount
//              and no less value.
//   CHANGE     output M+1 carries no token.
//
// Markers: @N@ @N_PLUS_1@ (numbers), @OUTPUT_COUNT_CHECK@, @M_VALUE@ and @M_PLUS_1_VALUE@
// (fixed M: the constants M+2, M, M+1; variable M: 3 <= outputs <= MMAX+2, and M = outputs - 2
// read from OP_TXOUTPUTCOUNT, so each verifier run may choose its own M), @V_MINTING_PUSH@,
// @GRAPH_ROOT_PUSH@, @SETTLEMENT_LOCK_PUSH@, @VERDICT_FLOOR@, @S3_LE_PUSH@,
// @COMMITMENT_SIZE_CHECK@ (pool: exactly 32 bytes; demo: non-empty),
// @DIGEST@ (pool: OP_SHA256; demo-m1: empty, the commitment IS the digest),
// @LOOP_INIT@ and @ACCUMULATE@ (fan-out shape (a) or (b), see the loop).
//
// This shipped build substitutes only pool mode. Demo substitutions remain in
// the historical research prototype, outside the deployment builder.

//@check LAYOUT
OP_INPUTINDEX <@N@> OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
OP_TXINPUTCOUNT <@N_PLUS_1@> OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
OP_TXOUTPUTCOUNT @OUTPUT_COUNT_CHECK@
//@end

//@check OWN_TOKEN
OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY @V_MINTING_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end

//@check GRAPH_ROOT
<0> OP_UTXOBYTECODE @GRAPH_ROOT_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end

// The verdict loop: stack [acc j], j = 0..M-1. Fan-out shape (a), distinct
// verdicts: acc = C_0 ‖ … ‖ C_{j-1}. Shape (b), root copies: acc = C_0 and every
// C_j must equal it (the aggregate then commits one Merkle root R = C_0).
@LOOP_INIT@
OP_BEGIN
//@check VERDICTS
  OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY <32> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP OP_EQUALVERIFY
  OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTTOKENAMOUNT <0> OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
  OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE @SETTLEMENT_LOCK_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
  OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTVALUE <@VERDICT_FLOOR@> OP_GREATERTHANOREQUAL OP_VERIFY
//@end
  OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTTOKENCOMMITMENT
//@check COMMITMENT_SIZE
  @COMMITMENT_SIZE_CHECK@
//@end
  @ACCUMULATE@
  OP_1ADD OP_DUP @M_VALUE@ OP_NUMEQUAL
OP_UNTIL
OP_DROP

//@check STATEMENT
@DIGEST@
<1> OP_SPLIT OP_SWAP 0x011f OP_AND OP_SWAP OP_CAT OP_REVERSEBYTES
0x024c84 OP_SWAP OP_CAT @S3_LE_PUSH@ OP_CAT
<0> OP_INPUTBYTECODE <66> OP_SPLIT OP_DROP OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@ablated OP_DROP
//@end

//@check FACTORY
@M_VALUE@ OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY OP_EQUALVERIFY
@M_VALUE@ OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOBYTECODE OP_EQUALVERIFY
@M_VALUE@ OP_OUTPUTTOKENCOMMITMENT <0> OP_EQUALVERIFY
@M_VALUE@ OP_OUTPUTTOKENAMOUNT <0> OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY
@M_VALUE@ OP_OUTPUTVALUE OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOVALUE OP_GREATERTHANOREQUAL OP_VERIFY
//@end

//@check CHANGE
@M_PLUS_1_VALUE@ OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY OP_SIZE OP_NIP OP_NOT
//@ablated <1>
//@end
